.TH CHIBICC 1 "September 2026" "REM developer tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
chibicc \- compile C source for the REM Linux target
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chibicc
[-S|-c] [-O0|-O2] [-g] [-I dir] [-D macro] [-o output] \fIinput.c ...\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chibicc
is the native REM C compiler driver. It parses C and emits REM assembly or
invokes the configured REM assembler and linker. A hosted static executable
requires the matching REM CRT objects, musl headers and libc, libgcc archive,
and user linker script. These pieces must come from one validated runtime
tuple.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -S
Emit assembly rather than linking.
.TP
.B -c
Compile/assemble to an object without linking.
.TP
.B -O0, -O2
Select the supported unoptimized or optimized mode.
.TP
.B -g
Request debug information. Tested builds do not all provide complete
source-level DWARF data.
.TP
.B -I dir, -D macro
Add an include directory or preprocessor definition.
.TP
.B -o FILE
Choose the output path.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
chibicc -S -o hello.s hello.c
chibicc -c -o hello.o hello.c
chibicc -O2 -static -o hello hello.c
./hello
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The REM driver uses \fBCHIBICC_REM_AS\fR, \fBCHIBICC_REM_LD\fR,
\fBCHIBICC_REM_LINKER_SCRIPT\fR, \fBCHIBICC_REM_CRTDIR\fR, and
\fBCHIBICC_REM_GCCLIB\fR to select the matching runtime components.
.SH LIMITATIONS
The tested REM subset is smaller than full hosted C11. Consult
REM_C_COMPILER_STATUS.md and REM_VALIDATED_RUNTIME_TUPLES.md before selecting
language/library features or mixing toolchain files.
.SH SEE ALSO
as(1), ld(1), remdbg(1)
